            <div xml:id="d843">

                <pb facs="0733" n="724" sameAs="frus:frus1940v02/pg724"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">346B.115 Standard Oil Co./10: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Minister in Egypt</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Fish</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1940-10-24T19:00:00-05:00">October 24, 1940—7
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>127. Please inform the Saudi Arabian Government through the appropriate channel
                    that your Government today protested to the Italian Government through the
                    Italian Ambassador in Washington the bombings by Italian aircraft in the night
                    of October 18, 1940, of the property of the California Arabian Standard Oil
                    Company at Al Khobar in Saudi Arabia.</p>
                <p>You should add in your communication to the Saudi Arabian Government that your
                    Government would appreciate being informed of the attitude which the Saudi
                    Arabian Government may take or has taken concerning this violation of its
                    neutral rights.</p>
                <p>Repeat to Baghdad for its information.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
